codex
Triage result: this can be built only as Track B. Theorem 15 proves PPAD/query hardness for the paper’s recursively reduced circuit/oracle distribution, not for an inverse-planted coloring; the paper also explicitly identifies boundary bichromatic search as easy. I’ll therefore make the efficient route visible in the metadata and benchmark a compactly encoded native Sperner coloring whose planted trichromatic unit triangle is known before the coloring circuit is assembled.
STEP 0 supports a native Track B family: exact Sperner witnesses verify cheaply, but no average-case Track A claim is justified for a planted distribution. The family will disclose and measure its efficient recurrence algorithm.
  ✓ Read the full paper and triage G/H/V, including Track A vs B costs
  ✓ Inspect repository harness contracts and existing utilities
  → Implement and validate the generator, or write a reviewable rejection
  • Run selftests, hardening, and G9 arms; write final artifacts
codex
The module is now implemented around the continuous 2-simplex, with exact rational coordinates and a checker that never reads the planted answer. The first full gate run is exercising 200,000 structure-aware triangle guesses plus relabelling invariance; this is also stress-testing whether the richer rational witness format remains practical.
