The corrected construction is now mathematically clean: every planted triangle is a valid paper-style continuous-simplex witness at exact distance \(2^{-b}\), the coloring satisfies the Sperner boundary condition, and the transition is unique. The only failing gate is deliberately G9 because zero oracle attempts were scored. I’ve written the README, machine-readable self-test report, and a `BLOCKED.md` that gives the exact rerun procedure without misclassifying the paper as rejected.
