G1–G8 pass. The shipping candidate has one valid answer among 2,147,483,647 structure-aware candidates; 200,000 guesses produced zero hits. The nine-element answer uses 79 characters, and the intended route is bounded by 160 exact operations.

Completion is blocked by OpenRouter: every bare, hinted, and placebo call returned HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded`. These errors are preserved in the transcripts and were not counted as model failures. Consequently, G9 and `all_passed` remain false, and the result must not be submitted until OpenRouter quota is restored and the three oracle runs are repeated.

The README also documents an off-by-one inconsistency between Definitions 5 and 9 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.15713) and the exact dyadic interpretation used by the generator.
