paper_src/hardness-warmup.tex:44:\begin{definition}[2{\rm D}-\rect\Sperner]
paper_src/hardness-warmup.tex:47:    In $2${\rm D}-\rect\Sperner, we are given coloring $C:Q^2_n \to [3]$ satisfying: (1) $C(x,0)\in \{1,2\}$ and $C(x,2^{n}-1)=3$ for any $x\in Q_n$; and (2) $C(0,0)=1, C(2^n-1,0)=2$, and $C(0,y)=C(2^{n}-1,y)=3$ for any $y\in Q_n\setminus \{0\}$. 
paper_src/hardness-warmup.tex:48:    The goal of $2${\rm D}-\rect\Sperner is to find $\vec{x^*}\in ( Q_{n}\setminus \{2^n-1\}  )^2$ such that $|\settxt{C(\vec{x}): x_i \in \settxt{x_{i}^*,x_{i}^*+1} }|=3$.
