The Step 0 scan already rules out the naïve interpretation: “plant a colorful simplex in an explicit coloring table” would expose a polynomial scan and has no compact-vs-mechanical distinction. I’m now checking the paper’s circuit/oracle formulation and its tight easy boundary (two colors) to see whether a native Track B construction can preserve the promised coloring while hiding a trichromatic witness behind a short invariant.
