Step 0 supports a native Track B family, but not the original planted-simplex idea. I’m using the paper’s own 2D-rect Sperner object (Definition 23): a succinct coloring circuit with one trichromatic unit square. Its direct circuit evaluation takes a million recurrence/reflection steps at the shipping preset, while a Fibonacci alternating-sum invariant reduces the route to under 160 exact operations. The paper’s two-color binary-search observation is explicitly accounted for rather than hidden.
