# Blocked on mandatory oracle evidence

The corrected generator passes local gates G1–G9(c), but it is not release-ready.
The old constant-affine prototype was discarded because ordinary matrix powering
already solved its recurrence in `O(log n)`, eliminating the claimed Track-B cost
gap. The retained generator instead uses a time-varying fractional-linear circuit
with a moving-pole cross-ratio identity.

The required bare hardening run and both isolated G9 diagnostic runs were attempted
against that corrected module on 2026-09-05. Each harness made four calls/redraws;
all twelve returned HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded (total limit)`. The harness
correctly counted none as a solver failure and terminated without a verdict. The
script-owned records remain in:

- `llm_loop_transcript.jsonl`
- `g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl`
- `g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl`

When OpenRouter quota is restored, rerun the bare command. If it hardens, rerun the
two G9 arms in their isolated directories, update `G9_ORACLE_RESULTS`, regenerate
`selftest_report.json`, and revise the README tables. Do not write `REJECTED.md`:
